Kubernetes Deployment Strategies:

Choosing the right deployment strategy is key to minimizing downtime and risk. Here's a quick guide:

✅ Rolling Update (Default)  
- Gradually replaces pods one-by-one  
- Best for: Most production apps  
- Challenge: Slow rollback if issues surface late  

⚡ Recreate  
- Kills all old pods before starting new ones  
- Best for: Non-critical apps, staging  
- Challenge: Causes downtime -- not ideal for production 

🔵 Blue-Green  
- Runs old + new versions simultaneously  
- Switches traffic instantly  
- Best for: Zero-downtime needs  
- Challenge: Double resource cost  

🧪 Canary  
- Releases to a small user subset first  
- Expands after monitoring  
- Best for: Safe production testing  
- Challenge: Needs advanced traffic routing & monitoring 

---

🛠️ Choosing the right strategy depends on:

Your app’s tolerance for downtime

Rollback needs

Infra capacity

Monitoring & observability maturity


Plan smart → Test early → Monitor always! 🔍
